WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.734
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:07.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.734 --> 00:00:09.067
Well, guys, earlier today,

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.200
President Biden made
a major announcement

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.300
that he is banning U.S. imports
of Russian oil,

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.601
dealing another huge blow
to Russia's economy.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.601
Yeah, this is devastating
for Russia.

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:22.000
Now their biggest export is
bad guys in "John Wick" movies.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.067
[ Russian accent ] You'll never
get away with this, John Wick.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:31.400
[ Normal voice ]
Of course, we've got to get oil
from somewhere else,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.901
which is why today Biden looked
at Rudy Giuliani and was like,

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:35.100
"Let's get you in the sauna,
buddy.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.834
Let's go."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.767
"Let's get you
on the treadmill, pal."

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.801
That's right, gas prices
were already on the rise,

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.701
and with the decision
to ban Russian oil,

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.634
they're higher than ever before.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:50.400
Gas prices are so high,
the Indy 500 was just changed

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.067
to the Indy 5.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:55.367
Gas prices are so high,
this morning, parents were like,

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:56.601
"Alright, kids, we're Amish now.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.767
Let's get in the buggy.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.734
We're taking the horse
to school."

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.033
Gas prices are so high,

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.701
Americans are just filling
their cars with Red Bull

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.100
and hoping for the best.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:06.801
Listen to this --
According to a new poll,

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.367
70% of Americans support a ban
on Russian oil,

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:13.100
even if it means
higher gas prices.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.534
Yeah, then Netflix was like,
"We're also raising our prices

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:18.467
to help Ukraine.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:20.100
Gonna help Ukraine."

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.467
Meanwhile, in another blow
to their economy,

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.367
today, McDonald's announced
that it was closing

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.934
all 850 of its restaurants
in Russia.

00:01:29.934 --> 00:01:33.000
Yeah, we don't want their oil,
and they can't have our grease.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:35.701
That's right.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.868
Not to be outdone,
Arby's announced

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.234
that they are punishing Russia
by staying open.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.567
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.868
Yeah, they're open 24/7.
Yeah.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.667
-"We have the meats."
-Yeah, McDonald's --

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:50.801
McDonald's in Russia
is a little strange.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.968
It's the only country
that sells Unhappy Meals.

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:54.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.667
Oh, gosh.
Yeah.

00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:59.000
Just give me the card, yeah.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.534
Can I sign it?

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:07.667
♪♪

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.567
Here you go.
How you doing?

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.801
There you go.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:12.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:15.901
Just terrible.
I had to do that joke.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.801
Thank you.
I had to do that joke.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.334
Sorry.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:21.300
"Unhappy Meals."
-Nice. Come on.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.601
-I apologize, everyone.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.167
Some more business news.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:27.167
Apparently to offset
rising costs,

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:31.200
toilet paper brands are cutting
back on the size of their rolls.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.634
Yeah, whether it's
a global pandemic or a war,

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:35.300
they always have to
make it about them.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.734
It's always about toilet paper.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.067
Yeah, it's not good.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:43.300
Today at CVS, I saw a package
of Charmin Just Tubes.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:48.167
-Wow.
-What do you do with it?

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.400
-Wow.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.133
Guess they wiped out the supply.

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:55.701
[ Rim shot ]

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.501
-You're on a roll.
-Yeah.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:58.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:04.033
♪♪

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.200
-Well, some TV news --
last night was our favorite

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.367
"The Bachelor:
Women Tell All" episode.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:10.701
And things got pretty heated

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.400
after Shanae
called out Genevieve

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.701
for hooking up with
a former "Bachelor" contestant.

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.167
The show can be
pretty emotional,

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.167
so I thought we could help.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.400
Here's the moment re-voiced

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.267
with the least emotional person
we know -- Siri.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:25.567
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:28.868
-"Let's get Siri-ous."

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.267
-After I got eliminated,
I went home.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.133
And then when you
get eliminated,

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.934
you bleep Aaron
from Katie's season.

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:37.200
What? What?

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.901
Whoa. Oh.
Oh, my God.

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.901
Oh, you know what?
You know what's funny? Oh, okay.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:44.033
I know you've been DM'ing him
and all that.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:47.133
100%. Go ask him, 'cause I've
never slid in his DMs, honey.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:48.534
He sent me a screenshot, honey.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.501
I never slid in his DMs.

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.901
No.
I've never slid in his DMs.

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:54.334
Ha ha ha ha.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.834
